# Research summary

## Problem

In infrastructure-less mobile ad-hoc networks, nodes relay packets for one another while the topology changes. Routing decisions can affect reliability, network throughput and latency.

## Compared protocols

| Protocol | Category | Core idea |
|---|---|---|
| AODV | Reactive | Discover routes on demand using request/reply messages |
| OLSR | Proactive | Maintain topology and reduce flooding using multipoint relays |
| DSDV | Proactive | Maintain distance-vector routing tables with sequence numbers |

## Question

How do AODV, OLSR and DSDV compare on packet delivery, packet loss, throughput and end-to-end delay as network size changes from 20 to 30 to 50 nodes?

## Contribution

A comparative NS-3 simulation study reported at IEEE GCAT 2022. The research is about wireless-network performance; it is **not** an AI or healthcare application.

